<title>USA: Calpine cuts estimated price terms of proposed IPO.</title>
<headline>Calpine cuts estimated price terms of proposed IPO.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calpine Corp has cut the estimated price per share in its proposed initial public offering to $17 to $20 from its initial proposal of $18 to $21, according to a regulatory filing.</p>
<p>The San Jose, Calif., company generates electric and steam power. The number of shares to be offered, 18,045,000, remains unchanged.</p>
<p>The company has proposed to trade on the New York Stock Exchange under the symbol &quot;CPN.&quot; The offering is expected sometime this week.</p>
</text>
